# module Maven vendored integration

Detect root `pom.xml` and consume `maven` exports only with a locked vendor. The export name is
`group:artifact`; its vendored POM path should be explicit so preflight does not need the tree.

# decision Generated reactor plus precise root POM blocks

The wholly tool-owned `deps/git-a2a.maven/pom.xml` is a sorted aggregator of vendored module
paths. The consumer POM receives a marked module entry for that aggregator and one marked
dependency per module; existing XML outside markers stays byte-identical. A container created by
git-a2a is marked and removed when empty. Foreign generated content is discarded with a warning.

# invariant Reactor versions must match

The managed dependency uses `${project.version}` because Maven composite substitution does not
exist. The consumer reactor and vendored artifact must publish the same version; Refresh exposes a
mismatch as a native Maven build error rather than silently installing or rewriting the library.

# test Golden and real-toolchain lifecycle

Goldens cover existing containers, repair, drift, and byte-restoring Unwire. Integration runs
`mvn -B package -DskipTests` against a copied vendored Java module and compiles a real consumer.
